prompt:
Build a text adventure engine in Python as a package adventure/ with adventure/__init__.py, adventure/world.py and adventure/engine.py.
- adventure/world.py: load_world(path) reads a JSON file like {"start": "hall", "rooms": {"hall": {"description": "A dusty hall.", "exits": {"north": "kitchen"}, "items": ["key"], "locked": {"north": "key"}}}} and returns it as a dict ("items" and "locked" may be missing: treat them as empty). A start room that does not exist, or an exit to a room that does not exist, raises ValueError.
- adventure/engine.py: class Game(world) starting in the start room, with game.room (the current room's name) and game.inventory (a list). command(text) -> str (case and extra spaces do not matter):
  look -> the description, then a line `Exits: east, north` (sorted, or `Exits: none`), then a line `Items: key, lamp` if the room has items (in the room's order);
  go DIRECTION -> moves and returns what look returns; `You can't go that way.` if there is no exit; `The way north is locked.` if that exit is locked and the player does not carry the item it needs;
  take ITEM -> `Taken: key` (moved from the room to the end of the inventory) or `There is no key here.`;
  drop ITEM -> `Dropped: key` or `You don't have key.`;
  inventory -> `You carry: key, lamp` or `You carry nothing.`;
  anything else -> `I don't understand.`
Write unit tests too.
